From 6c289a5e07ebd3ce9c39b72b17d98796493d4f6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <57wsdx6b8d@privaterelay.appleid.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:49:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let the bottom bar show the toolbar buttons it does not have

The top toolbar can offer Share, Translate, Bookmark and others through its
adaptive optional button, but only ever one at a time, and only at the top.
The bottom bar has room for several and is where the thumb already is. The
actions themselves are not the problem; the two surfaces just describe a
button differently. The optional button hands out a ButtonData when asked,
while a bottom bar action publishes a PropertyModel that its binder observes.

Rather than write a second Share that would slowly drift from the first, this
reads one and writes the other. BareButtonDataActionAdapter subscribes to an
existing provider, asks it about the current tab, and copies the answer into a
model registered under a new ActionId. The provider keeps its owner: the
adaptive toolbar still builds it and still destroys it, and nothing about how
it behaves changes by being read a second time.

Reaching the provider needs an accessor, since the controller keeps its
providers to itself. AdaptiveToolbarButtonController, AdaptiveToolbarUi-
Coordinator and RootUiCoordinator each gain one lookup by variant, returning
null when that variant was never built.

Providers hold the active tab as a plain supplier and never watch it, leaving
that to whatever displays the button. The adapter therefore observes the
activity tab itself and re-asks the provider on every change, including the
tab that is already in front when it starts.

Three actions go through it: Share, Translate and Bookmark. Share is always
applicable, Translate only on some pages, and Bookmark carries state, so
between them they ask the adapter every question a page action can ask. Of the
two similar flags on the spec only isSelected is copied, because it is the one
that means what IS_SELECTED means here; isChecked drives a contextual page
action appearance the bottom bar has no equivalent for. Bookmark turns out to
carry its state by swapping its whole ButtonSpec between an outline star
reading "Bookmark this page" and a filled one reading "Edit Bookmark", so
copying the icon and the description carries it without the adapter knowing
what a bookmark is.

The provider builds each icon once and the top toolbar is already showing it,
so the adapter hands the bar a copy. Handing over the same Drawable would have
been handing it over rather than sharing it: setting an image tint mutates the
Drawable, and a Drawable reports back to only one view, so the two surfaces
would have fought over the colour and one would have stopped redrawing.

The bar itself can now put any of these anywhere. Three of its five positions
are the user's to arrange, and the whole bar is resolved at once rather than a
position at a time, because the buttons are held in a map keyed by action and
the same action twice is impossible rather than merely odd. Slots resolve left
to right and an earlier one wins; a slot that cannot keep what is stored falls
back to what it does by default, and then to the first action in the catalogue
nothing else is using. Stored rubbish, a stale action from another build, and
the same action in every slot all resolve to a usable bar.

What made a position special has moved to the action that position used to
hold. The view an action is drawn into, the binder it is drawn through and the
id that view carries are all chosen from the action now, so Home takes its long
press menu wherever it goes, the app menu takes its update badge, and neither
leaves anything behind for whatever replaces it. Home is still hidden when the
homepage is off and the shared slot is still shown only where it applies, but
both now follow the action rather than the position, so an ordinary action in
the first position does not vanish with the homepage and Home does not become
permanent by being moved out of it.

Nothing writes a preference, so a profile that has never been customised
resolves to the arrangement Bare shipped.
